# Docker build context for the ROOT context ("."), which is used only by
# steemdb-web/Dockerfile — it builds the SPA (steemdb-frontend/) and the Go
# API (steemdb-web/).
#
# The sync images build from ./steemdb-sync and are governed by
# steemdb-sync/.dockerignore, so nothing under steemdb-sync/ is needed here.
# Without this file a full-repo context carries local test-chain data
# (steemdb-sync/test/steem-test/data, hundreds of GB on a dev box), the host
# node_modules, and .git — none of which any stage COPYs, and all of which
# break or stall a build.

# Local chain data / test stacks: never part of a web image.
steemdb-sync/

# Version control and local runtime state.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github
.cursor
.multica
.zcode
issue-attachments

# Dependencies and build output: the image installs and builds its own
# (a host node_modules copied over the container's would carry glibc binaries
# into an alpine image).
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-ssr
bin/
**/*.test
**/*.out
**/*.exe
**/*.dll
**/*.so
**/*.dylib

# Logs, temp dirs and local secrets.
**/*.log
**/logs
**/tmp
**/temp
**/test-tmp
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/*.local.yaml
**/*.local.yml
**/*.secret.yaml
**/*.secret.yml

# Docs and container/orchestration files are not needed inside the image.
docs/
**/*.md
docker-compose*.yml
**/Dockerfile*
**/.dockerignore
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
